==Trivia==
*''Kuma'' (熊) is the Japanese word for bear.
*Antarctica (南極 ''Nankyoku'') is the only main Kumanchu Royale stage that does not appear in the English version of [[Empire of Cats]].
*Most of the [[Enemy Bases|enemy bases]] from Kumanchu Royale were reused for the English version of Empire of Cats. There are two exceptions besides Antarctica's:
**Japan in the English version of Empire of Cats uses Kyoto Prefecture's [[Media:Ec026.png|base]] from [[BCJP]] (a [[wikipedia:Maiko|''maiko'']] in front of [[wikipedia:Kinkaku-ji|Kinkaku-ji]]). Japan's base from Kumanchu Royale (the [[wikipedia:National Diet Building|National Diet Building]]) was instead repurposed for [[The Great Abyss (Into the Future)|The Great Abyss]], albeit with a redesign.
**The [[Moon (Empire of Cats)|Moon]] in the English version of Empire of Cats uses an [[Media:Ec047 en.png|English-localized version]] of Iriomote's Island's [[Media:Ec047 ja.png|base]] from BCJP (a tree), leaving the original Moon base unused. In [[The Battle Cats POP!]], however, the Moon stage uses a similar but shorter version of the one from Kumanchu Royale. [[File:TBC POP! Moon base.png|thumb|100px|The Moon's base in The Battle Cats POP!]]
*In Kumanchu Royale's title screen, [[Cambodia (Empire of Cats)|Cambodia]]'s base had a coppery tint rather than a mix of gray and green.
*[[Higher Score|Challenge Battle]] was the only stage to appear in both [[Ganso!! Nyanko Daisensou]] and Kumanchu Royale, albeit with different enemies in each game.
*The Omni Strike, Multi-Hit and Kamikaze abilities would not return until The Battle Cats Versions [[Version 5.5 Update|5.5]], [[Version 6.0 Update|6.0]] and [[Version 6.7 Update|6.7]], respectively.
*Most of the new enemies were based on different cultures or myths.
*[[Ursamajor]]'s Japanese name, Kumanchū (クマンチュー), may be derived from ''Kumanchu Royale'' and 宇宙 ''uchū'' (outer space; the cosmos).
*It is heavily implied that the [[Mooth]] in The Battle Cats is the son of the Mooth from Kumanchu Royale. The Battle Cats Mooth's Japanese description says he was hoping to become a beautiful butterfly in the future and was once a delinquent, while the Kumanchu Royale Mooth's description says he hopes his child becomes a beautiful butterfly in the future without becoming a delinquent, instead of living the same life as its father.
*When Muscle Bear or Tank Bear hits a [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] enemy, a unique attack effect appears.

